title: What you do now, once your server runs the new code
pid: 134942d6-8f29-43f9-a622-eb3792dfe64e
body: |2-
  The same gesture as for any other child. In your fork's view,
  a4555e5b-9d20-4141-8470-06cefcad2ed4, under the root write
  '** x ⟨node:REPLY-ID⟩', then
  'save FILE --port 1761', read the report, 'save FILE --port 1761 --yes';
  delete that headline and its subtree, and save the same two ways.
  The hide is recorded against your original message, not his reply:
  the fork's 'H' count grows by one, and '1H' shows on your original
  (9ea7da6a-f4a0-4a4c-8bc9-a1c8a457f861 and
  12c6e3ab-f99b-44cb-a93e-0981c86f36fe for the two replies you tried).
  Until then, the old binary does the same if you place and remove the
  original's ID instead of the reply's.
